[[File:Jug of wine detail.png|left|130px]]
'''A jug of wine''' is a type of [[Drinks|drink]] that restores 11 [[Hitpoints]] and temporarily lowers [[Attack]] by 2, leaving behind an empty [[jug]] after consumption. It can be obtained by using [[grapes]] with a [[jug of water]], requiring level 35 [[Cooking|Cooking.]] The process of fermenting takes 12 seconds, but if another jug of wine is created within this time period, the 12 seconds restart. When the process is finished, all unfermented wine in the player's inventory or bank will ferment. Each jug of wine grants 200 Cooking [[experience]], but every jug that fails to ferment becomes a [[jug of bad wine]] instead. The fail rate decreases as the player's Cooking level increases, and it will stop failing entirely at Cooking level 68.

Jugs of wine can be blessed at the [[exposed altar]] in [[Ralos' Rise]] to create a [[jug of blessed wine]] (which cannot be banked).

The [[Culinaromancer's Chest]] sells both jugs and grapes and has a nearby sink for filling the jug, making it an ideal location for creating jugs of wine. They may also be purchased, with the closest shop to a bank being [[Sunlight's Sanctum]] in [[Aldarin]] which offers an unlimited supply. Furthermore, there is a [[bank deposit box]] outside this bank, closer to [[Sunlight's Sanctum]] than the bankers.

Wine is notable for its affordability and accessibility which makes it a popular low cost food, especially for activities that do not excessively utilise [[run energy]] as it is notably heavy. Making wines is also a cheap and effective method of training Cooking; for more details, see [[Pay-to-play Cooking training#Levels 35/68–99: Jug of wine|here]].  

[[File:Making jug of wine.gif|thumb|right|160px|A player creating a jug of wine.]]

