==Success chance==
The chance for an unfermented wine to successfully turn into a jug of wine is about 60% at level 35, increasing to a 100% chance at level 68.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1424083965883961350|date=7 August 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/101801|archivedate=7 March 2023|quote=19% - 138% (values 100% and above mean guaranteed success)
A stack of wines is divided into batches, rather than rolling for each one individually, which means that the outcomes often won't represent the real chance as accurately as one might expect.}} Note that while mixing large quantities of wine at the same time, rolls are not made for each jug of wine individually. Rather, the total amount of unfermented wines is divided into 15 batches, with a skilling success roll being performed for each of them, in addition to the unfermented wines left over from the division.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1424496857611481094|date=8 August 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/97499|archivedate=7 March 2023|quote=I think it's 15 batches, plus individual rolls for the remainder that didn't make it into those batches.}} Any potential levels gained from successfully processing earlier batches are not taken into account for the success rate of ensuing batches.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/859438300041490432|date=2 May 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/108816|archivedate=7 March 2023|quote=Unfortunately so, yes. The amount of code it had to run when it tried to let your level-change take effect was more than the game could run.}}
